# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=gift spec=priest:discipline style=melee
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=844x390,touch save=carried (behaves as
# fresh, #273 -- carried never actually carries across separate playbot
# invocations because the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
# `boss=gift` is a coverage label only (direction.md's 2026-09-25 note on
# playpick.ts): a mode=walk evening steers at no named boss, the walk starts
# at the door same as any other.
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: checked sessions.jsonl -- the only prior
# mode=walk/melee evening on record is 2026-09-25-25 (rogue:assassination,
# 10-normal). This is the first melee-style evening at 25-heroic, and the
# first melee-style pairing with a healer at all (priest:discipline has only
# ever been run under flee/idle/wander before now). melee has no away-from-
# danger term (direction.md's 2026-09-26 tank-melee note: it beelines at
# hud().boss and walks straight through ground hazards), so a healer forced
# to close to melee range of every pack and boss for a whole heroic evening,
# never casting a heal from a safe distance, is the strictest test this line
# has put a healer through yet -- and #267's bonestorm-punishes-proximity
# finding was found on a tank; this asks whether a healer pays the same way.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:priest:discipline
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot arrive-threshold

evening melee 200 6
state
shot after-evening
says
bill
